[Music]  hi  i'm curator emily allred and i want to  welcome you all to drawing games  chess posters from around the world one  of our summer exhibitions here at the  world chess hall of fame  this exhibition has over 100 chess  posters on a variety of subjects  mostly drawn from the collection of the  world chess hall of fame  and they're from over 100 countries this  exhibition  is really unique like really uniquely  encapsulates  our mission here at the world chess hall  of fame which is not just to  talk about the history of the game of  chess but also the art and culture of it  and so if you'll join me as we kind of  walk around the gallery you'll get to  see  a little bit of chess culture from  around the world  so we'll start over here which is a wall  of  posters about the chess olympiads and  as many of you know the chess olympiads  are team competitions  in which people from around the world  represent their home countries and this  year they did it virtually  but many years or most years it's  on different sites around the world and  so these  posters kind of uniquely represent local  cultures  you'll see this one which is from a  chess olympiad in the philippines  and it has the national bird of the  country  in the poster carrying a king piece in  front of the philippine  flag there are others where  they talk about kind of the mythology of  the country  or even have local landmarks like this  giant  camel bearing a rook on its back which  is an actual sculpture in dubai that was  created for  the chest olympiad there but still  stands today  we'll go ahead and take a look at some  of these other chest posters  which are from the most important chess  competitions around the world  the world chess championships so this  pair  of um of posters take two  very different kind of approaches to  representing the most important  competition in the chess world so  one distills the stakes of the the  competition  to a crown representing you know the  king of the chess world  the highest honors while the other  represents the drama  of the 1972 world chess championship in  which  um kind of this american  brash player is challenging boris baskey  who represented the soviet union and  they had dominated the chess world  since the end of world war ii and here  bobby is carrying his sack of cash he's  dressed as a cowboy on a night  and he's trying to snatch the crown from  boris baskey and the crown  has hammer and sickles probably  representing that soviet dominance of  the crown  and there are other figures you know  peering around  watching him and it just kind of  uniquely portrays that drama you know we  have the sister organization the st  louis chess club across the street so  big chess tournaments  are happening you know usually every  year and so we're kind of capturing  chess history here as it's happening  in st louis and these posters  represent that these are posters from  competitions held here on the st louis  chess campus  we have the 2019 junior chess  championship  we have the women's chess championship  and then  the karen's cup which was the last big  tournament we had here on campus this  year before  kovid 19 restrictions went into place  and these are all signed by the  competitors  and so you know we sell these in queue  boutique as well but it's kind of nice  to have these in our collection  as mementos of these really important  events  we also have a poster that we recreate  every year  for the new hall of fame inductions and  it portrays  each of the new inductees to the world  in the us chess halls of fame  thank you all for attending our virtual  tour of drawn games  chess posters from around the world i  hope that we'll get to see you here in  st  louis at the world chess hall of fame  sometime in the future  you

